{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,18]],"date-time":"2026-06-18T04:55:50Z","timestamp":1781758550807,"version":"3.54.5"},"reference-count":32,"publisher":"Oxford University Press (OUP)","issue":"1","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2025,1,16]],"date-time":"2025-01-16T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1736985600000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":14,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100000770","name":"University of Manchester","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100000770","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100000271","name":"STFC","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100000271","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100004543","name":"China Scholarship Council","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100004543","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":[],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,1,2]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>ABSTRACT<\/jats:title>\n               <jats:p>We present high-resolution e-MERLIN and EVN (e-VLBI) observations of a radio source associated with Dyson Sphere candidate G, identified as part of Project Hephaistos. The radio source, VLASS J233532.86\u2212000424.9, is resolved into three compact components and shows the typical characteristics of a radio-loud active galactic nucleus (AGN). In particular, the European VLBI Network (EVN) observations show that it has a brightness temperature in excess of $10^{8}$\u2009K. No radio emission is detected at the position of the M-dwarf star. This result confirms our earlier hypothesis, that at least some of the Dyson Sphere candidates of project Hephaistos are contaminated by obscured, background AGN, lying close to the line of sight of otherwise normal galactic stars. High-resolution radio observations of other Dyson Sphere candidates can be useful in distinguishing truly promising candidates from those contaminated by background sources.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1093\/mnrasl\/slaf006","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,1,16]],"date-time":"2025-01-16T02:34:41Z","timestamp":1736994881000},"page":"L56-L61","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":3,"title":["High-resolution imaging of the radio source associated with Project Hephaistos Dyson Sphere Candidate G"],"prefix":"10.1093","volume":"538","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-4988-3513","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"T","family":"Ren","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Jodrell Bank Centre for Astrophysics, Department of Physics and Astronomy, School of Natural Sciences, University of Manchester , Oxford Road, Manchester M13 9PL ,","place":["UK"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-6714-9043","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"M A","family":"Garrett","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Jodrell Bank Centre for Astrophysics, Department of Physics and Astronomy, School of Natural Sciences, University of Manchester , Oxford Road, Manchester M13 9PL ,","place":["UK"]},{"name":"Leiden Observatory, Leiden University , PO Box 9513, NL-2300 RA Leiden ,","place":["The Netherlands"]},{"name":"Institute of Space Sciences and Astronomy, University of Malta , Msida MSD2080 ,","place":["Malta"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-2828-7720","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"A P V","family":"Siemion","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Jodrell Bank Centre for Astrophysics, Department of Physics and Astronomy, School of Natural Sciences, University of Manchester , Oxford Road, Manchester M13 9PL ,","place":["UK"]},{"name":"Breakthrough Listen, Astrophysics Sub-Department, Department of Physics, University of O